# renderer.js

Build pages as HTML strings, then assign `document.body.innerHTML`. Follow `renderFeedPage` and `buildPostHTML`. Do not introduce a virtual DOM or JSX.

- Read listings from `{pathname}.json` with `credentials: 'include'`. Comment pages arrive as a two-item array.
- Sidebar data comes from `/r/{name}/about.json`. Skip `all`, `popular`, and `friends`.
- Writes go to `/api/vote`, `/api/save`, `/api/hide`, `/api/comment`, and `/api/submit` as form bodies. Send `uh` from `currentModhash` or `getCookie('csrf_token')`.
- Thing ids are fullnames on `data-fullname` (`t3_`, `t1_`).
- After feed, comment, or profile HTML is inserted, call `attachInteractiveListeners`.
- `purgeShredditStyles` must not remove `#subreddit-custom-css`.

```js
// ❌ BAD — JSON body, anonymous request
await fetch("/api/vote", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ id: fullname, dir }),
});

// ✅ GOOD — session cookie plus modhash
const bodyParams = new URLSearchParams({ id: fullname, dir: String(dir), uh });
await fetch("/api/vote", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" },
  credentials: "include",
  body: bodyParams.toString(),
});
```
